        "title": "Forming Techniques - Blowing, Casting, Drawing, Pressing",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Glass can be shaped by any technique that exploits its viscous behavior in the working range. Every major forming technique maps to a specific viscosity window — too hot and the glass won't hold form, too cool and it won't move. The revolution of glass blowing (~50 BCE) was that it made glass forming fast and accessible; the IS machine (1925) made it industrial."
    },
